                    <item>
                <title>Best Buy sells Blu-rays online and in-store again</title>
                <link>https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/best-buy-sells-blu-rays-again-after-quitting-the-business-in-2024/</link>
                                    <comments>https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/best-buy-sells-blu-rays-again-after-quitting-the-business-in-2024/#comments</comments>
                
                <dc:creator>
                    <![CDATA[Scharon Harding]]>
                </dc:creator>
                <pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:31:17 +0000</pubDate>
                		<category><![CDATA[Tech]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[best buy]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Blu-ray]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[dvd]]></category>
                <guid isPermaLink="true">https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/best-buy-sells-blu-rays-again-after-quitting-the-business-in-2024/</guid>

                                    <description>
                        <![CDATA[Popular titles like <em>The Odyssey</em> are being “sold &#038; shipped by Best Buy."  ]]>
                    </description>
                                                                <content:encoded>
                            <![CDATA[<p>Best Buy is selling Blu-rays directly through its website and in physical stores again after exiting Blu-ray and DVD sales in 2023.</p>
<p>The Best Buy website’s movie section currently lists 15 Blu-rays (including one two-pack) that are “sold &amp; shipped by Best Buy.” New titles available include <a href="https://arstechnica.com/culture/2026/08/review-yes-were-still-arguing-about-nolans-the-odyssey/"><em>The Odyssey</em></a> (2026), <a href="https://arstechnica.com/culture/2026/03/project-hail-mary-is-in-theaters-but-do-the-linguistics-work/"><em>Project Hail Mary</em></a> (2026), <a href="https://arstechnica.com/culture/2026/07/review-supergirl-is-not-the-disaster-its-low-box-office-suggests/"><em>Supergirl</em></a> (2026), <em>Super Mario Galaxy</em> (2026), and <em>Obsession</em> (2025). Best Buy is also selling some older titles on Blu-ray, including <em>It’s a Wonderful Life</em> (1943), <em>Saving Private Ryan</em> (1998), and <em>The Godfather</em> (1972).</p>
<p>Most of the Blu-rays are available for purchase online and can be delivered to an address or picked up at a Best Buy store within a few days. As of this writing, <em>The Odyssey</em> appears to be in stock at Best Buy stores, as it’s currently listed as available for pickup within as little as an hour.</p><p><a href="https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/best-buy-sells-blu-rays-again-after-quitting-the-business-in-2024/">Read full article</a></p>
<p><a href="https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/11/best-buy-sells-blu-rays-again-after-quitting-the-business-in-2024/#comments">Comments</a></p>
]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                    
